From 2a5defb2ff75e18ef795c8a083734aded0736c8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:26:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban chat links: the owner publishes its hub
 subscriptions' chat links, so a chat's task list does not wait on its own
 sync

During laptop-1's Board sync outage (sync role given up, SchemaAhead, 2026-11-13) a chat placed six cards on
worker-2/4/7 and the hub. Their done notices arrived (hub.db `sessions` links), but with
`kanban.sync.links_reader: replica` the chat's task list, sidebar counts and ask-gate read only Board
`task_chat_links` rows, which only the chat's own gateway wrote (from its origin ledger) through the sync that was
down. None of the six cards had a row.

The owner's links pass now turns each counted `platform='hub'` subscription `<gw>/<profile>/<session>` on an open
card it owns into an unreleased link row for that chat (`_owner_hub_links`): the same subscriptions hermes-hub
publishes as the card's `sessions`, so notices and the task list read one membership.

- Same uid the chat's gateway writes for that link (`created` when the card carries a courier origin intent, the
  ledger's `via: origin`; `shepherd` otherwise), so the recovered gateway upserts this row, never a second one.
- Insert-only, once: nothing is written while any row for that card and chat exists in the board file or the
  replica, released included, so a release the chat's gateway made is never reopened. An unreadable replica writes
  nothing that pass. Touch/send_refused subs, placeholder and worker sessions, and the owner's own chats are skipped.
- The chat's gateway releases these rows when the card closes: `_owner_written_releases` now covers `shepherd`
  as well as `created`.

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_chat_links_owner_hub_subs.py): two gateways on one fake Board, the chat
gateway's sync given up the real way (PR #2033's fixture). A courier-placed card is in `session_tasks` once, counted,
with a clean links_diff after one replica pull (fails on main); after the sync recovers there is still exactly one
unreleased row; a card done during the outage is released by the recovered gateway; filtering and
never-reopen/unreadable-replica cases. Live proof on scratch homes with the real CLI (`kanban origin-create`,
`kanban sync links/run`, `kanban chat-tasks --expect`): exit 4 on main, exit 0 with this change.

Card: t_01a1d44d87ea4bef
